    "LDAP, Kerberos, and SMB traffic to 172.17.0.17 and domain controllers is normal enterprise AD activity (benign queries, not exploitation)"
  ],
  "incident_summary": "Windows workstation BEPOSITIVE (172.17.0.99) belonging to domain user afletcher is infected with Koi Stealer malware, confirmed by Suricata signature match. The malware maintains persistent command-and-control communication with 79.124.78.197 via HTTP POST requests to /foots.php every 30-60 seconds. The compromised host also attempts lateral movement by sending SMB exploitation payloads (NTMLSSP unicode overflow, IPC$ share access, transaction DOS) and Kerberos attacks to 172.17.0.17."
